## Vulnerability Analysis (CVE-2021-25646)

The vulnerability allows attackers to bypass JavaScript security settings via the empty key `""`. When Java code is compiled without the `-parameters` flag, `@JsonCreator` constructor parameters with `@JacksonInject` have empty names. Jackson's `@JacksonInject` defaults `useInput=DEFAULT` which allows JSON input matching the parameter name to override injected values. The empty `""` JSON key matches the unnamed `@JacksonInject JavaScriptConfig` parameter, letting attackers inject `{"enabled": true}` to bypass the server's JavaScript-disabled config.

